            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>When to Use This SOP</h2>
<p>Managing multiple overseas ad accounts often leads to scattered top-up records, mismatched spend data between your finance system and platform reports, missing invoices at month-end, and manual Excel reconciliation that consumes hours of your team's time.</p>
<p>This document provides a step-by-step Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) for reconciling ad spend, top-ups, and invoices across Meta, TikTok, and Google Ads. Save it for easy reference.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Step 1: Account Binding &amp; Basic Setup</h2>
<p><strong>Objective</strong>: Centralize all ad account data in your financial management tool to prevent top-up and spend information from scattering across platforms.</p>
<p><strong>Actions</strong>:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Compile an Account Inventory</strong></li>
<li>Export all ad account information: Account ID, Account Name, Platform (Meta Business/TikTok Business/Google Ads), Targeting Region, Agency/Account Owner</li>
<li>Mark which accounts are direct client accounts vs. sub-agency accounts</li>
<li>
<p>Maintain this list in a shared online spreadsheet; update it whenever new accounts are added</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Enable Platform Billing Notifications</strong></p>
</li>
<li><strong>Meta Business</strong>: Set up a billing email to receive invoices at a centralized finance email address</li>
<li><strong>TikTok Business</strong>: Bind a billing email in 「Account Settings」</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Google Ads</strong>: Enable 「Billing Notifications」 email alerts</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Configure Financial Reconciliation Tools</strong> (Optional but Recommended)</p>
</li>
<li>Use 以渔's account management features to automatically sync top-up records</li>
<li>Or integrate your finance system's API for automated data pulling</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>Step 2: Standardize the Top-Up Process</h2>
<p><strong>Objective</strong>: Ensure every top-up has documentation, with one-to-one correspondence between top-up amounts and account balance changes.</p>
<p><strong>Actions</strong>:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Pre-Top-Up Confirmation</strong></li>
<li>Check the current account balance</li>
<li>Verify the top-up amount aligns with your budget plan</li>
<li>
<p>Record the reason (e.g., new campaign launch, activity-period scaling, low balance warning)</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Execute the Top-Up</strong></p>
</li>
<li>Top up via 以渔's platform or directly on the ad platform</li>
<li>
<p>Save the top-up receipt screenshot (including top-up time, amount, transaction ID)</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Post-Top-Up Verification</strong></p>
</li>
<li>Refresh the account balance within 5 minutes to confirm receipt</li>
<li>Record in your reconciliation sheet: Date, Platform, Account, Amount, Transaction ID, Operator</li>
<li>If using a Prepaid Management Account (PMA), additionally record consumption transfer records</li>
</ol>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>⚠️ Note</strong>: Some ad platforms (e.g., Meta) may have delays in crediting top-ups. Allow buffer time to avoid campaign pauses due to delays.</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2>Step 3: Track Spend Data</h2>
<p><strong>Objective</strong>: Monitor spend across accounts in real-time and promptly identify anomalies or data discrepancies.</p>
<p><strong>Actions</strong>:</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Daily Spend Monitoring</strong></li>
<li>Log into each ad platform and export the previous day's spend report</li>
<li>
<p>Key metrics: Daily total spend, day-over-day change, budget cap triggers</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Weekly Data Aggregation</strong></p>
</li>
<li>Every Monday, aggregate the previous week's account spend data</li>
<li>Compare 以渔's backend records with platform reports to check for discrepancies</li>
<li>
<p>If variance exceeds 5%, investigate causes (timezone differences, data latency, attribution windows)</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Spend Anomaly Alerts</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
