<hr />
<h2>FAQ</h2>
<p><strong>Q1: How long does it take to see the balance after a top-up?</strong><br />
A: Typically instant crediting. Some platforms (e.g., Meta) may have a 5-15 minute delay. If not credited within 30 minutes, contact your agency or platform support.</p>
<p><strong>Q2: What if platform report data doesn't match backend records?</strong><br />
A: First, verify timezone settings (platforms typically default to the advertiser account timezone). Second, check data update times (spend data may have a 24-hour delay). If discrepancies persist, submit a platform ticket.</p>
<p><strong>Q3: Is it compliant if the invoice issuing entity doesn't match the contract entity?</strong><br />
A: Some ad platforms are served by different legal entities; invoice issuers may differ from the charging account. Confirm the invoicing entity before signing contracts and establish corresponding relationships in your finance system.</p>
<p><strong>Q4: What special considerations exist for Prepaid Management Account (PMA) reconciliation?</strong><br />
A: PMA accounts require additional attention to consumption transfer records—funds transferred from PMA to sub-accounts should be separately recorded to avoid mixing with top-up amounts. Recommend setting up two independent fund pools in your system for management.</p>
<hr />
<h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
<p>The core of unified reconciliation lies in three points: <strong>data centralization</strong> (all accounts, top-ups, and spend records managed in one place), <strong>process standardization</strong> (fixed operational steps and timing), and <strong>traceability of anomalies</strong> (every discrepancy has records and follow-ups).</p>
<p>Following this SOP, you can complete the previous month's reconciliation by the 5th of each month, reducing financial reconciliation time from days to hours. If you encounter specific issues during operations, feel free to contact 以渔's team for further support.</p>
